export anchor BroadcastControlStyle:
    number: 358
    screen: VideoEditor
    name: Broadcast control
    idea: The editor as a television control room multiviewer, a black wall of tiles each named by an under monitor label with a tally box, the program tile ringed red and marked ON AIR, sources as small monitors with level meters, and the timeline as a rundown strip.
    base: dark
    palette:
        wall: #000000, the monitor wall and gaps between tiles
        tile: #08080a, tile faces and the style sheet
        umd: #1b1b1f, under monitor label bars, header cells and list rows
        button: #26262c, transport and secondary buttons
        ink: #f2f2f2, text
        muted: #a9a9b2, field names and track roles
        tallyRed: #ff3b30, program ring, ON AIR dot and the playhead
        exportRed: #d92a20, Export button and playhead tag behind white text
        onAirText: #ff5c52, the ON AIR word
        tallyGreen: #30d158, preview ring, PVW tag and play
        readout: #7dff9a, inspector values
        amber: #ffb000, the clock, the router badge and focus
        cue: #ffcc4d, durations and the cut to logo marker
    type:
        Labels use a condensed stack, Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed,
        Liberation Sans Narrow, Arial, at 14px, bold and tracked 0.1em in
        under monitor labels. Numbers use a mono stack. The clock is mono
        40px bold in amber, readouts mono 14px in green, durations mono
        12px. The program title card is system sans 600 up to 32px.
    layout:
        A router strip on top shows Brightwork Cut on an amber block, then
        cells SHOW Launch teaser, FMT 1080p and RATE 24 fps. The wall is a
        four column grid of black tiles with 2px gaps. Program spans two by
        two on the left, ringed with a 3px red inset frame, and its label
        bar reads a red disc, PGM, LAUNCH TEASER and a red ON AIR. Four
        source tiles fill the right, SRC 1 to SRC 4, each a small monitor
        with a simple picture or a pair of green level meters, and a label
        bar with a flat dash tally, the file name and an amber duration. The
        third row holds SRC 5 with the logo, a preview tile ringed green
        with an engineering table of POSITION 960 x 540, SCALE 100 percent,
        OPACITY 100 percent and X DISSOLVE 12 FR and a label PVW TITLE CARD
        V2 SELECTED with a hollow green square, and a two column clock tile
        with the amber timecode, TRT and the duration, three flat transport
        buttons with a green play, RENDER with an empty bar and 0% STANDBY
        with a hollow square, and a red EXPORT block. A rundown tile spans
        the full width with track rows, clips as dark blue or dark green
        bars with a bright left edge, the selected title clip outlined green
        with a green PVW tag, an amber diamond CUT TO LOGO with a dotted
        line and a red playhead with a red 18 tag. At phone width only
        program, clock and rundown remain.
    spacing: 2px gaps between tiles, 8px to 14px inside tiles. Nothing else.
    density: High. Eight tiles and a rundown strip fill the wall.
    corners: Square everywhere, except the round ON AIR tally.
    borders: Tally rings are 3px inset frames, red for program and green for preview.
    shadows: None. Light comes only from the tiles.
    icons:
        Tally shapes are the main icons. A filled disc is on air, a hollow
        square is preview or standby, a flat dash is idle. Each sits beside
        a word. Transport uses filled glyphs.
    focus: A 3px amber outline offset 2px.
    tone: Control room shorthand in capitals, such as PGM, PVW, SRC 1, TRT and STANDBY.
